"""Goods and the processes that make them.

One row = one good + its primary production process. Columns:

  id | name | cat | unit | kg/unit | world price (2025 W$/unit) | inputs | equipment | labor | knowledge | options

inputs     `good:qty` per unit of output. `a/b/c:qty` = substitutable inputs
           (the producer uses the cheapest one it can get).
equipment  primary capital good (or land/deposit), then `+aux:ratio` = auxiliary
           capital needed per unit of primary. `@rate` fixes output per unit of
           primary equipment per month; otherwise it is calibrated from the
           capital share of value added.
labor      `occupation:weight`. Hours are calibrated so that at 2025 frontier
           wages labor takes `vas` (default 55%) of value added. `lx=` scales
           hours (older, labor-intensive technologies).
knowledge  knowledge nodes that must be understood to design/make it.
options
  need=group:weight:income_elasticity   household consumption
  svc       service: not storable, produced when sold
  local     only sold inside the producer's region
  nt        not internationally tradable
  tol=um    tightest dimensional tolerance in micrometres. The maker's
            equipment precision must be within 4x of it; yield falls with the gap.
  clean=id  cleanroom facility required (cleanroom_iso7/5/3)
  prec=um   (capital goods) precision this machine delivers when used
  life=m    service life in months (capital goods & consumer durables)
  dep=x     extracts deposit x from the region (resources.py)
  co2=t     tonnes CO2 emitted per unit
  opq=0..1  how opaque the product is to reverse engineering
  alt=trad  also generate a traditional labor-intensive process
  lx/kx     labor / capital intensity multipliers
  restricted  the world will not export it (strategic technology)
"""

